❯ Create path-scoped rule files under .claude/rules/ (use the paths:            
  frontmatter so each                                                           
  rule only loads for matching files). Base them on the installed Cognine       
  coding-standards                                                              
  plugins; keep each file short and imperative.                                 
                                                                                
  1. backend-python.md (paths: backend/**/*.py)                                 
     - snake_case modules/functions, PascalCase classes, UPPER_SNAKE constants, 
  booleans                                                                      
       start with is_/has_/should_/can_; files under ~500 lines                 
     - routers orchestrate only; business rules in services; DB access only in  
  repositories;                                                                 
       inject via Depends; never instantiate external clients inside business   
  functions                                                                     
     - full type hints, mypy --strict clean, Google-style docstrings on public  
  functions                                                                     
     - Pydantic v2 schemas with extra="forbid" for request models               
     - custom exception hierarchy in core/exceptions.py mapped to consistent    
  JSON errors                                                                   
     - structured logging, no PII (no full receipt text in logs)                
  2. api-design.md (paths: backend/src/app/routers/**)                          
     - REST resource naming, plural nouns, /api/v1 prefix, correct status       
  codes,                                                                        
       pagination params (page, size), consistent error envelope {code,         
  message, details}                                                             
  3. frontend-react.md (paths: frontend/src/**/*.{ts,tsx})                      
     - PascalCase components, useX hooks, camelCase services/utils; max line    
  100                                                                           
     - components render only; logic in hooks; HTTP only in services via shared 
  Axios client                                                                  
     - server state via TanStack Query only, never in Zustand; Zustand only for 
  auth/session                                                                  
     - forms with React Hook Form + Zod; no any; props typed and documented     
     - accessibility: semantic HTML, labels on inputs, keyboard navigable       
  4. security.md (paths: backend/, frontend/src/)                               
     - upload validation: allowed MIME (image/jpeg, image/png,                  
  application/pdf), magic-byte                                                  
       check, max size from settings, randomized stored filenames, never trust  
  client name                                                                   
     - secrets only via env/.env (never committed); .env.example kept current   
     - role checks via dependency on every admin route; employees only access   
  own receipts                                                                  
  5. testing.md (paths: backend/tests/, frontend/src//*.test.tsx)               
     - pytest naming test_<feature>_<scenario>_<expected_result>; tests mirror  
  source tree                                                                   
     - mock only external boundaries (LLM/OCR client, filesystem, clock)        
     - in-memory/temporary SQLite per test; factories for test data             
     - target >= 80% backend coverage on services                               
  6. git-workflow.md (no paths: always loaded)                                  
     - Conventional Commits, branch names feature/AICC139-<short-desc>          
                                                                                
  After creating them, list each file with a one-line summary.                  

