● Both skills are created. Here are the two SKILL.md files:

  1. .claude/skills/fastapi-react-feature-scaffold/SKILL.md

  ---
  name: fastapi-react-feature-scaffold
  description: Scaffold a brand-new domain feature/resource end-to-end across a
  FastAPI + SQLAlchemy + Alembic backend and a React + TypeScript + Vite
  frontend. Trigger when the user asks to "add a new feature", "add a new
  resource/entity", "scaffold a CRUD endpoint", or names a new domain noun that
  needs backend + frontend plumbing (e.g. "add an Invoice feature"). Do NOT
  trigger for edits to an existing feature's files — only for creating a new
  one. Project-agnostic: reusable across any FastAPI + React codebase that
  follows a routers/services/repositories backend and a feature-sliced frontend.
  ---

  # FastAPI + React Feature Scaffold
  ...
  (generation order: schema -> model -> repository -> service ->
  router+registration -> alembic migration
   -> backend tests -> frontend types -> service -> hook -> component ->
  frontend test;
   placeholder table; rules while generating; final checklist: ruff/black, mypy
  --strict,
   alembic upgrade head, pytest, eslint/tsc, vitest, no leftover placeholders,
  router reachable)

  Templates live under templates/backend/ (schema, model, repository, service,
  router, test_service, test_router) and templates/frontend/ (types, service,
  hook, component, component test), all using {{Name}}/{{name}}/{{name_plural}}
  placeholders.

  2. .claude/skills/receipt-extraction/SKILL.md

  ---
  name: receipt-extraction
  description: Domain knowledge and procedure for this project's receipt
  extraction and categorization pipeline — the canonical extracted-field schema,
  the ReceiptExtractor strategy interface, field validation rules, and
  categorization logic. Trigger when working on anything under
  backend/src/app/extraction/, adding or modifying a receipt extractor, writing
  validation for extracted receipt fields, implementing expense category
  suggestion, or writing tests against receipt data. Do NOT trigger for generic
  CRUD features unrelated to extraction — use fastapi-react-feature-scaffold for
  those.
  ---

  # Receipt Extraction
  ...
  (canonical schema: merchant_name, receipt_date, subtotal, tax_amount, 
  total_amount,
   currency, line_items[], confidence{}, raw_text; ReceiptExtractor interface +
  how to add
   a new extractor; validation rules: total≈subtotal+tax tolerance, date not
  future,
   ISO-4217 currency, confidence threshold -> needs-review; categorization:
  keyword/merchant
   map first, LLM suggestion second with confidence, categories always from DB;
  fixtures list)

  Fixtures under fixtures/: clean_restaurant_receipt.json (valid, no review),
  total_mismatch_needs_review.json (total ≠ subtotal+tax),
  foreign_currency_future_date.json (EUR, future date — both exercise the "needs
  review" path).

  Full file contents are on disk at the paths above if you want to open and
  tweak them directly.

