● Created both subagents under .claude/agents/:

  1. standards-reviewer.md — tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash (no Edit/Write).
     Reviews changed code against .claude/rules/*.md and the two Cognine
     plugins, runs ruff/mypy/bandit/eslint/tsc/npm audit/pip-audit via Bash
     only, and writes a Mandatory/Recommended/Nitpick report with file:line refs
     to docs/reviews/review-<date>-<scope>.md. Explicitly forbidden from fixing
     anything.
  2. test-engineer.md — tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, but scoped
     by instruction to test files only (backend/tests/**, **/*.test.tsx). Writes
     pytest/Vitest+RTL tests per testing.md, mocks only the
     extractor/LLM/filesystem/clock boundary, runs suites with coverage, and
     reports any bug it finds instead of fixing it.

  Both have description fields starting with "Use PROACTIVELY after any
  feature/bugfix is implemented..." so Claude Code auto-delegates to them
  post-implementation, plus explicit trigger phrases a user might type.

