❯ Implement Claude Code hooks in .claude/settings.json with scripts in          
  .claude/hooks/                                                                
  (Python scripts, cross-platform, read the hook JSON from stdin).              
                                                                                
  PRE-hook (PreToolUse):                                                        
  - matcher "Edit|Write|MultiEdit": block (exit code 2 with a clear stderr      
  message) any                                                                  
    write to .env, *.db / *.sqlite files, uploads/ directory, or                
  alembic/versions files that                                                   
    already exist (existing migrations are immutable).                          
  - matcher "Bash": block destructive commands (rm -rf on root/home/project     
  root,                                                                         
    git push --force, DROP TABLE, deleting the sqlite db) and secret leaks      
  (echo of                                                                      
    ANTHROPIC_API_KEY etc.).                                                    
  - Log every blocked attempt to .claude/logs/hooks.log with timestamp and      
  reason.                                                                       
                                                                                
  POST-hook (PostToolUse):                                                      
  - matcher "Edit|Write|MultiEdit": if the edited file is .py under backend/,   
  run                                                                           
    ruff check --fix and black on it, then mypy on it; if .ts/.tsx under        
  frontend/,                                                                    
    run prettier and eslint --fix on it. If problems remain, return them to     
  Claude                                                                        
    (exit code 2 with the errors on stderr) so it fixes them immediately.       
  - Append a line per run to .claude/logs/hooks.log.                            
                                                                                
  Also add a Stop hook that prints a reminder if backend tests haven't been run 
  this session.                                                                 
  After creating, demonstrate both: try to edit .env (should be blocked), then  
  edit a                                                                        
  Python file with bad formatting (should be auto-fixed). Record the output in  
  docs/evidence/hooks.md.                                                       

