● Everything is set up and verified end-to-end. Summary:

  Created in .claude/hooks/ (all Python, stdlib-only, cross-platform, read hook
  JSON from stdin):
  - hook_common.py — shared log()/block()/allow() helpers writing to
    .claude/logs/hooks.log
  - guard_writes.py (PreToolUse, Edit|Write|MultiEdit) — blocks .env/.env.*,
    *.db/*.sqlite*, anything under uploads/, and edits to an existing
    alembic/versions/*.py file (new migrations still allowed)
  - guard_bash.py (PreToolUse, Bash) — blocks rm -rf on root/home/project,
    Remove-Item -Recurse -Force, git push --force/-f (but not
    --force-with-lease), DROP TABLE, deleting the sqlite db, and echoing
    secret-like env vars (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, etc.)
  - format_and_lint.py (PostToolUse, Edit|Write|MultiEdit) — runs ruff check 
    --fix → black → mypy on changed backend .py files, or prettier --write →
    eslint --fix on changed frontend .ts/.tsx files; exits 2 with remaining
    errors on stderr if any survive
  - track_test_runs.py (PostToolUse, Bash) + stop_test_reminder.py (Stop) —
    together implement the "pytest not run this session" reminder via a
    per-session marker file

  Wired into a new .claude/settings.json.

