● Root cause is actually earlier: assigning receipt.line_items = [...] on an
  already-flushed object triggers a synchronous lazy-load of the old collection
  value, which fails under async. The real fix is to build the Receipt fully in
  memory before the first add()/flush. Let me fix upload().

  Read 1 file (ctrl+o to expand)

