    _MISSING_GREENLET_BUG_REASON constants), since the underlying bug is fixed.
    The one unrelated, genuine xfail (regex-parsing bug in
    text_fallback_extractor.py) was left untouched.

  Verified: pytest --cov=app → 115 passed, 1 xfailed, 0 failed, 93% coverage;
  mypy --strict src and ruff check src tests both clean.

  Standards-reviewer result

  2 mandatory findings (both verified real):
  - dependencies/auth.py:32 queries the DB directly instead of via
    UserRepository.get_by_email — a layering violation.
  - categorization_service.py:157 instantiates the Anthropic client inline per
    call instead of injecting it.

  I caught and corrected one inaccurate finding in the subagent's draft: it
  claimed a mypy --strict failure in core/security.py:39, which I
  reproduced-tested twice (including with --no-incremental) and could not
  confirm — PyJWT 2.13 ships inline types, so the return is already str, not
  Any. I removed it from Mandatory and documented the discrepancy transparently
  in the report rather than passing along a false finding.

  5 recommended items and 3 nitpicks are also logged (dependency CVEs in
  pyjwt/pillow/react-router-dom/zod, a repository→service import inversion, a
  possible dangling category_id on update, and an auth race in the frontend's
  login flow).

  Remaining gaps

  - The 2 confirmed mandatory findings above are unfixed (out of scope for this
    task per "do not revisit completed features" — they're new findings from
    today's review, not from the prior completion report, so I'm flagging rather
    than fixing).
  - playwright MCP remains uninvoked all session (documented, not reconnected).
  - Dependency version bumps (pyjwt, pillow, react-router-dom, zod) are
    unresolved, per the review's Recommended section.

  All of the prior completion report's gaps (stale xfails, missing
  docs/reviews/, missing reusable-skill evidence, undocumented MCP status) are
  now closed.

